            <ArticleTitle>[On the importance of the reflectory-segmental effects for the combined treatment of knee joint osteoporosis in the patients of advanced age].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.17116/kurort2016116-20</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present article demonstrates the role of reflectory-segmental effects during baro-laser therapy for the treatment of arthrosis of the knee joints in elderly patients. It has been shown that the additional treatment of the lumbosacral region while applying baro-laser therapy in the patients of the advanced age significantly enhances their functional capabilities including the increase of duration of painless walking and the reduced intensity of the pain syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
